model {
  extend basalt.modelGateway {
    metadata {
      constraint "Pool availability monitoring is absent from deployment until an explicit target is configured. A one-minute cron reads that pool's uncached account view, durable acknowledgement and exact native revision without warming, renewing, reconciling, installing or dispatching inference. Failed renewal remains visible even while acknowledged policy serves through grace. Runtime and view failures cannot suppress the separate guard observation. Each run has a bounded deadline and sends paired check-ins to an existing monitor, with fixed guard and reason diagnostics on failure. Cron incident envelopes carry the Worker release and a bounded runtime observation from the same passive probe, including observed boot, running state and selected application version when known. An expected selected boot stays separate from an observed boot. Legacy runtime APIs expose no application version, and Worker image configuration is not proof of the running image, so unavailable identities remain explicit. Sampling adds no runtime or provider reads and never suppresses an outage. Privacy verification rejects private diagnostic values and invalid status sentinels in every envelope field, while accepting measured durations containing the same digits. Monitor creation, alert routing and production activation require a separately approved exact target plan."
    }
  }
  extend basalt.poolRuntime {
    metadata {
      constraint "The management-authenticated native policy check runs the scheduler admission predicate against its current immutable registry and a fresh signed revision assertion with no candidates. It does not install policy, extend a deadline, select an account, refresh the plugin health lease or issue inference. The separate runtime health lease remains required. Unknown, dirty, expired and different revisions refuse this check."
    }
  }
}
